============================================================
COMPLETENESS PRESSURE: TOURNAMENTS vs GENERAL DIGRAPHS
============================================================

  At n=5:
    Tournament arcs: 10 = 10 (FIXED)
    Degrees of freedom: 10 (one bit per pair)
    Total tournaments: 1024 = 1024
    Achievable H values: [np.int64(1), np.int64(3), np.int64(5), np.int64(9), np.int64(11), np.int64(13), np.int64(15)]
    Missing odd values: [7]

  THE RIGIDITY INTERPRETATION:
    H=1: 0 cycles. Freedom: 10 arcs. UNDERCONSTRAINED.
    H=3: 1 cycle.  Freedom: 7 arcs.  UNDERCONSTRAINED.
    H=5: 2 cycles. Freedom: 4 arcs.  UNDERCONSTRAINED.
    H=7: 3 cycles. Freedom: 0 arcs.  RIGID → forced 5-cycle → H≥9.
    H=9: 4 cycles. Freedom: reborn (5-cycle adds new DOF).

    7 is the UNIQUE odd value at the rigidity threshold.
    It is the value where the system transitions from
    'underconstrained' to 'overconstrained', and the
    overconstrained system forces H to jump past 7.

